# CA certificates that images built with luthersystems/build-harden must not
# trust. One certificate per line:
#
#   <sha256 of the DER> <root|intermediate> <PEM file in ca-distrust/> <source> <name>
#
# A root is removed from every trust store. An intermediate is not in a trust
# store; it is blocked where the TLS stack has a block list (Java
# blocked.certs, NSS, the Red Hat p11-kit blocklist), and the image check
# fails if one still verifies against any trust store in the image. List each
# certificate a key has (a cross-signed copy is another certificate), so a
# chain through another root is blocked too.
#
# modules/ca-distrust.sh checks each PEM against its fingerprint before it
# uses it. Add an incident's certificates at the end, under a comment that
# names it.

# CVE-2026-111943 (October 2026): the keys of eight eMudhra intermediates leaked
# (EM DV/OV/EV TLS CA and EM OV CS CA, G3B and G3C). Each has an
# emSign-issued and a Sectigo "AAA Certificate Services" cross-signed copy
# with the same key (Bugzilla 2083449). The emSign roots above them go too:
# the four in Mozilla's set before NSS 3.131.1 and the two G3 roots that
# issued the intermediates, with their cross-signs from ECC Root CA - G3.
bc4d809b15189d78db3e1d8cf4f9726a795da1643ca5f1358e1ddb0edc0d7eb3 root emsign-ecc-root-ca-c3.pem crt.sh/?id=713606976 emSign ECC Root CA - C3 (issuer: emSign ECC Root CA - C3)
86a1ecba089c4a8d3bbe2734c612ba341d813e043cf9e8a862cd5c57a36bbe6b root emsign-ecc-root-ca-g3.pem crt.sh/?id=713604941 emSign ECC Root CA - G3 (issuer: emSign ECC Root CA - G3)
